-- PaintMasks (Round 7 C-02, rebuilt in Round 8 C-04; generated, do not edit by hand): where each car may be painted, and what every
-- other part of its texture is. One 256 x 256 region map per car texture, run-length coded in base64: each run is two bytes, the
-- region value in the high nibble of the first byte and the run length minus one in the low nibble plus the second byte.
-- Values: 1 to 6 = body panel (dark to bright shade, the car's own light and shade); never painted: 8 glass, 9 light, 10 tyre or
-- rim, 11 trim (chrome, grille, bumper, plate, sign, rack), 12 interior or underside, 13 other (0 = unused texture). The cars are
-- one mesh each (body and glass together), so the map is cut from each car's own texture (tools/paint-masks: colour clusters per
-- car, a hand-written spec per car, then region clean-up so the edges are smooth) and checked on the car in Studio.
-- Gold and Diamond editions share the Normal car's mesh, so they use the same mask; each Rainbow edition has its own mesh and
-- texture, so its entry is keyed "Rainbow <car>".

